itz on M, whose values are returned. The dense solver below 64","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, or when k is a third of them or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"largest","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", every weight is finite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and nonnegative, and "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}]}],"name":"Precondition"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run spends "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" products without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging, with the products spent and the largest Ritz residual on the tolerance’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scale. The dense solver throws as "},{"code":"adjacencySpectrum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Throws"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\